<title>USA: Charlotte County, N.C., rejects gasoline tax.</title>
<headline>Charlotte County, N.C., rejects gasoline tax.</headline>
<dateline>CHARLOTTE, N.C. 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>North Carolina's Charlotte County Commission has rejected a proposed 5-cents-a-gallon tax on gasoline, county officials said.</p>
<p>The proposal failed in a 2-2 vote Tuesday. It could be revived if a reconsideration vote is called by Commissioner Mac Horton, who was absent from Tuesday's meeting.</p>
<p>The tax would have raised $3 million annually to fund road improvements.</p>
<p>((--Jane Sutton, 305-374-5013))</p>
